              "fill": "$color-accent-4",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 816,
              "content": "Notch a corner of the image to tuck in a caption. The inverse radius of the notch is $radius-large (24px). The notch snaps to the grid: it spans whole columns plus the gutter after them, so the image resumes at the next column. It hugs its text, up to half of the image's own columns — 10 of 20 for wide images, 6 of 12 for content images, 3 of 6 on mobile. Longer text wraps instead of widening the notch.",
